{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to audit successful and unsuccessful changes to /etc/inventory.conf using key inventory-config. The rule and audit service persisted across a verified node restart, and the file was restored unchanged after testing.","actions_performed":["Installed Alpine audit userspace packages.","Persisted `-w /etc/inventory.conf -p wa -k inventory-config` in `/etc/audit/audit.rules`.","Enabled and started auditd.","Verified permitted and denied writes were logged with the required key.","Restarted node1 once and verified boot identity changed, auditd recovered, and post-restart auditing remained operational."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent keyed audit rule","command_ids":["cmd-8d4fedcc988a49a1","cmd-62d62e2030a94d51","cmd-90c901a526fd4f3a"],"summary":"Shows the exact persistent and live rule, auditd enabled at boot and running, with zero lost events."},{"requirement":"Successful and unsuccessful changes recorded","command_ids":["cmd-94f75f5cb4e84c27","cmd-549d4b7c6fd346e3","cmd-c6d43683e3374b14"],"summary":"The permitted write succeeded, the unprivileged write failed with EACCES, and both appear as keyed audit events with success=yes and success=no respectively."},{"requirement":"Original inventory file preserved","command_ids":["cmd-94f75f5cb4e84c27","cmd-1132a8fbf8b340f1","cmd-90c901a526fd4f3a"],"summary":"Before/after hashes match after both test cycles; final mode is 644, owner root:root, and size 26 bytes."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-718a94e284ef455c","cmd-cc43d0afa46f438e","cmd-f8973b079a02440d","cmd-604850f85a4542b9","cmd-484b4c387c574438","cmd-90c901a526fd4f3a"],"summary":"Captures the healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered auditd/rule/data, and fresh post-restart successful and denied audit events."}]}
